From 030a94d2be416a96442e900fb9c624af954ae95a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Davide Palma (ElDavo)" <github@davidepalma.it>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:39:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] install: protect the recovery partition during zip installs

Zips for devices with a dedicated recovery partition often flash their
own recovery (LineageOS OTAs end with package_extract_file("recovery.img",
".../by-name/recovery")), replacing this recovery on every update.

While a zip runs, set the recovery block device read-only (BLKROSET) so
any write path fails (edify, dd, by-name or raw node), after snapshotting
it; afterwards clear the flag, compare, and write the snapshot back if
the partition still changed. Controlled by tw_protect_recovery (default
on), exposed in General settings and the install options on devices
with a recovery partition.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Wa3ghSNZcJdbnohyycUnSk
